f "/athletes/48673"} "Hiroko Nagasaki"] " who had the the best time in the world in 1983, 2:29.81. But she was bothered in LA by knee tendinitis and qualified only fifth. In the final Nagasaki and Ottenbrite went out in the lead, well ahead of Olympic record pace. But neither could maintain that pace, although Ottenbrite held on for the gold medal, coming home in 2:30.38. Nagasaki faded badly on the final lap and finished out of the medals in fourth. The silver went to American " [:a {:href "/athletes/51163"} "Susan Rapp"] ", who came from nowhere in the final 50. She was trailed by the surprising Belgian " [:a {:href "/athletes/45457"} "Ingrid Lempereur"] ", who came into Los Angeles with a PR of only 2:38.06, but improved that to 2:31.40 for the bronze."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "B Final"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "57"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/45852"} "Anne Ottenbrite"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/CAN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/CAN.png"}] "CAN"]] [:td {} "2:33.43 (2 h1)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "2:30.38 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "255"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/51163"} "Susan Rapp"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "2:33.46 (2 h2)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "2:31.15 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "29"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/45457"} "Ingrid Lempereur"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/BEL"} [